[00:01.50]As we can see from the picture,
[00:03.97]in a residence community with television antennas on the roof,
[00:08.82]an upset young man is talking to his friend 
[00:11.82]walking beside him along the street.
[00:14.55]It is apparent that the former assumes 
[00:17.55]that someone else is more qualified than him.
[00:20.68]Young people tend to give up when 
[00:23.68]the problem is beyond their ability to cope with.
[00:26.41]Superficially,
[00:27.80]it seems to be somewhat reasonable,
[00:30.77]but when weighing in the mind,
[00:33.24]we find there is an apparent tendency behind this phenomenon: 
[00:37.24]the lack of confidence.
[00:39.37]Firstly,
[00:40.16]it is well-known that we exist in a dynamic world 
[00:43.16]with various difficulties.
[00:45.50]We can do nothing but face them.
[00:48.87]Secondly,
[00:49.77]attitude is the key point of taking the first step.
[00:53.92]Being equipped with bravery 
[00:55.92]and confidence to solve the problem,
[00:58.87]you will find the question is not as “huge” as you imagine.
[01:03.62]So,
[01:03.92]with confidence and the right assessment of difficulties,
[01:07.87]try and exert our strength,
[01:10.14]and then we will overcome all the difficulties.
[01:14.10]On the whole,
[01:15.19]I believe we young people should face 
[01:18.19]the difficulties in a right manner.
[01:21.23]And nothing is impossible to a willing mind.
[ti:2-08-人生哲理类]